<div style="font-family: Arial, sans-serif;">
    <h1 style="background-color: #1a5276; color: white; padding: 15px 20px; text-align: center; border-radius: 8px; margin-bottom: 20px;">Lesson Planner – Theme # ___ – Lesson # 5</h1>
    <p style="text-align: center; font-style: italic; color: #555;">Complete this planner five times per theme, once per lesson (Lesson 1 through Lesson 5).</p>

    <h2 style="color: #1a5276; margin-top: 30px; margin-bottom: 15px;">SECTION 2 — LESSON IDENTIFICATION TABLE</h2>
    <table style="border: 1px dashed #333; border-collapse: collapse; width: 100%; margin: 10px 0;">
        <tr style="border: 1px dashed #333;">
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 10px; width: 50%;"><b>Lesson #:</b> 5</td>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 10px; width: 50%;"><b>Skills Focus:</b> Mediation</td>
        </tr>
        <tr style="border: 1px dashed #333;">
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 10px;"><b>Grade:</b> 11th Grade (CEFR: B1.2)</td>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 10px;"><b>Scenario:</b> Managing Stress in Changing Times</td>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 10px;"><b>Theme:</b> Forest Bathing and Other Biohacks</td>
        </tr>
        <tr style="border: 1px dashed #333;">
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 10px;"><b>Date(s):</b> From ___ to ___</td>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 10px;" colspan="2"><b>Learning Sequence Time:</b> 45–50 min</td>
        </tr>
        <tr style="border: 1px dashed #333;">
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 10px;" colspan="3">
                <b>Specific Objective:</b> Mediation: Communication: Resolve misunderstandings in group projects. Communication: Aid in negotiating group roles.
            </td>
        </tr>
        <tr style="border: 1px dashed #333;">
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 10px;" colspan="3">
                <b>Learning Outcome:</b> Mediation: Can resolve misunderstandings in group discussions about wellness practices by rephrasing statements and using gestures to guide focus (e.g., demonstrates a calming hand gesture and says, "Mindfulness means focusing on the present moment to reduce stress.")
                Can assist in assigning roles in wellness projects, ensuring that each classmate understands their responsibilities through visuals or examples (e.g., holds up a visual of relaxation techniques, and asks, "Would you like to cover relaxation techniques?")
                Can clarify group goals for wellness projects by using bilingual support and local examples (e.g., provides an infographic in both Spanish and English and explains, "Our goal is to share ways to manage stress with the class, such as visiting Parque Natural Metropolitano for nature walks.")
            </td>
        </tr>
    </table>

    <h2 style="color: #1a5276; margin-top: 30px; margin-bottom: 15px;">The Six Action-Oriented Approach (AOA) Lesson Stages</h2>
    <table style="border: 1px dashed #333; border-collapse: collapse; width: 100%; margin: 10px 0;">
        <thead>
            <tr style="background-color: #f2f2f2; border: 1px dashed #333;">
                <th style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 10px; width: 30%; text-align: left; color: #1a5276;">Stage & Description</th>
                <th style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 10px; width: 50%; text-align: left; color: #1a5276;">Activities & Teacher Actions</th>
                <th style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 10px; width: 20%; text-align: left; color: #1a5276;">Estimated Date and Time</th>
            </tr>
        </thead>
        <tbody>
            <tr style="border: 1px dashed #333;">
                <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 10px;">
                    <b style="color: #1a5276;">STAGE 1 — Warm-up / Pre-task</b>
                    <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">(Engagement, Modeling and Clarification)</p>
                </td>
                <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 10px;">
                    <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Warm-up:</b> "Stress-Buster Brainstorm" (5 min)</p>
                    <ul style="margin-bottom: 4px; padding-left: 20px;">
                        <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">The teacher displays images of natural settings (e.g., a serene forest, a peaceful beach) and people engaging in calming activities (e.g., meditating, practicing deep breathing).</li>
                        <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">Students are asked to quickly share one or two stress management techniques they've learned in previous lessons or practiced. They should use target vocabulary like 'relaxation,' 'mindfulness,' 'exercise,' or 'listening to music.'</li>
                        <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">Example prompts: "What helps you feel serene?" or "What's a beneficial habit for reducing stress?"</li>
                    </ul>
                    <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Modeling:</b> (5 min)</p>
                    <ul style="margin-bottom: 4px; padding-left: 20px;">
                        <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">The teacher models how to rephrase a concept or suggest a role politely.</li>
                        <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">Teacher (rephrasing): "If a classmate says, 'Forest bathing is just walking in the woods,' I could rephrase it like this: 'You mean *spending time in nature* to help *calm* your *mind* and *body*? It's more than just a walk; it's about making a sensory *connection* to natural elements for *stress relief*.'" (Focus on gerund: *spending*, *connecting*).</li>
                        <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">Teacher (suggesting a role): "For our video tutorial, *designing* the visuals is a big task. Alex, you *should try* to focus on that part because you're great with graphics." (Focus on gerund: *designing*, modal: *should try*).</li>
                        <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">Teacher emphasizes pronunciation of /uː/ in "soothing" and reduced vowels in "mindfulness."</li>
                    </ul>
                    <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Clarification (CCQs):</b> (3 min)</p>
                    <ul style="margin-bottom: 4px; padding-left: 20px;">
                        <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">CCQ1: "When I rephrase a statement, am I just repeating exactly what someone said, or am I explaining it in a different way to make it clearer for everyone?" (Expected answer: Explaining it in a different way to make it clearer).</li>
                        <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">CCQ2: "Why is it helpful to offer suggestions politely for group roles instead of just telling someone what to do?" (Expected answer: To encourage participation, show respect, and work together better).</li>
                    </ul>
                </td>
                <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 10px;"></td>
            </tr>
            <tr style="border: 1px dashed #333;">
                <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 10px;">
                    <b style="color: #1a5276;">STAGE 2 — Presentation</b>
                    <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">(Input of new language/content connected to Scenario)</p>
                </td>
                <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 10px;">
                    <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Material:</b> "Group Project Planning Session Transcript" (10 min)</p>
                    <ul style="margin-bottom: 4px; padding-left: 20px;">
                        <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">Genre: Informal dialogue/transcript. Register: Collaborative academic. Format: Written transcript of a group planning their "Stress Management Video Tutorial."</li>
                        <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">The transcript includes examples of initial misunderstandings about concepts (e.g., what "biohack" means), polite and impolite ways of suggesting roles, and vague project goals.</li>
                        <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">Key vocabulary: 'biohack,' 'mindfulness,' 'relaxation techniques,' 'promote wellness,' 'stress relief.'</li>
                        <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">Grammar focus: Modals for advice ("You should," "You could"), gerunds ("Practicing," "Listening").</li>
                    </ul>
                    <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Communicative Competence:</b> Can understand the main ideas of complex text on both concrete and abstract topics, including technical discussions in his/her field of specialisation.</p>
                    <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Comprehension tasks:</b></p>
                    <ul style="margin-bottom: 4px; padding-left: 20px;">
                        <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;"><b>Gist question:</b> "What is the main challenge this group is facing during their planning session?"</li>
                        <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;"><b>Identify Misunderstandings:</b> Students read the transcript and highlight phrases or concepts that seem unclear or misunderstood by group members.</li>
                        <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;"><b>Role Assignment Matching:</b> Match each group member's initial idea to the role they eventually considered, identifying where mediation might be needed to clarify or negotiate.</li>
                    </ul>
                </td>
                <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 10px;"></td>
            </tr>
            <tr style="border: 1px dashed #333;">
                <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 10px;">
                    <b style="color: #1a5276;">STAGE 3 — Preparation / Practice</b>
                    <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">(Accuracy focus on Mediation)</p>
                </td>
                <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 10px;">
                    <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Communicative Skill & Content:</b> Rephrasing statements, aiding in role negotiation, clarifying project goals. Grammar: Gerunds, Modals for advice, Present Continuous for trends. Vocabulary: breathing, relaxation, mindfulness, techniques, practice, reduce, improve, suggest, encourage, manage, focus, beneficial, effective.</p>
                    <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Detailed Procedure:</b> (12 min)</p>
                    <ul style="margin-bottom: 4px; padding-left: 20px;">
                        <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;"><b>1. Controlled Practice – Rephrasing for Clarity (5 min):</b>
                            <ul>
                                <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">Teacher provides 3-4 statements from the Presentation transcript that contain potential misunderstandings (e.g., "Forest bathing is just walking around trees." or "Biohacks are only for athletes.").</li>
                                <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">Students work individually or in pairs to rephrase these statements, making them clearer and more comprehensive, using gerunds and target vocabulary.</li>
                                <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">Example: Original: "Mindfulness is just thinking about nothing." Rephrased: "You mean *focusing* on the present moment and *observing* your thoughts without judgment to *reduce stress*? It's a *beneficial* practice."</li>
                            </ul>
                        </li>
                        <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;"><b>2. Semi-controlled Practice – Negotiating Roles (4 min):</b>
                            <ul>
                                <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">Teacher distributes dialogue strips with gaps for negotiating project roles. Each strip presents a scenario where a group member is unsure about their role or there's a conflict.</li>
                                <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">Students fill in the blanks using modals for advice (e.g., "You could...", "How about...?") and gerunds (e.g., "*filming* the intro," "*researching* techniques").</li>
                                <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">Example: "I'm not sure what to do for the video." -> "You *could try* *gathering* images of natural places. *Creating* visuals is important."</li>
                            </ul>
                        </li>
                        <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;"><b>3. Pair Interaction – Clarifying Project Goals (3 min):</b>
                            <ul>
                                <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">Students work in pairs. Student A makes a vague or incomplete statement about the "Stress Management Video Tutorial" project's goal (e.g., "Our video just needs to show some exercises.").</li>
                                <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">Student B practices clarifying the goal, rephrasing, and adding specific details, incorporating a local example or using bilingual support if necessary, as per the learning outcome. They can use gestures to guide focus.</li>
                                <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">Example: "Our goal is to share ways to manage stress with the class, such as *visiting* Parque Natural Metropolitano for nature walks." (Teacher encourages the use of a calming hand gesture while speaking).</li>
                            </ul>
                        </li>
                    </ul>
                </td>
                <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 10px;"></td>
            </tr>
            <tr style="border: 1px dashed #333;">
                <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 10px;">
                    <b style="color: #1a5276;">STAGE 4 — Performance / Production</b>
                    <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">(Communicative task where students USE the language in a realistic scenario)</p>
                </td>
                <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 10px;">
                    <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Task Format:</b> Group Project Planning and Mediation Simulation (10 min)</p>
                    <ul style="margin-bottom: 4px; padding-left: 20px;">
                        <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">Students work in their established "Stress Management Video Tutorial" groups. Each group receives a specific "mediation challenge" related to their project.</li>
                        <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">Examples of challenges:
                            <ul>
                                <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">"A group member thinks 'forest bathing' is silly and refuses to include it."</li>
                                <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">"Two members want to do the same core role (e.g., narrator), leading to conflict."</li>
                                <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">"One member is confused about what 'biohacks' are and suggests irrelevant content."</li>
                                <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">"The group goal is unclear; some think it's just about listing techniques, not demonstrating."</li>
                            </ul>
                        </li>
                        <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">Within each group, students take turns acting as the mediator, applying the skills practiced: rephrasing misunderstandings, using gestures for focus, politely suggesting and negotiating roles, and clarifying the project goals (e.g., "Our goal is to share ways to manage stress with the class, such as *visiting* Parque Natural Metropolitano for nature walks.").</li>
                        <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">Students must integrate gerunds (e.g., "Practicing mindfulness is key."), modals for advice (e.g., "You should consider..."), and present continuous for trends (e.g., "People are practicing deep breathing more often now.").</li>
                        <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">The teacher circulates, observing mediation strategies and providing support as needed.</li>
                    </ul>
                </td>
                <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 10px;"></td>
            </tr>
            <tr style="border: 1px dashed #333;">
                <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 10px;">
                    <b style="color: #1a5276;">STAGE 5 — Assessment / Post-task</b>
                    <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">(Formative assessment strategy)</p>
                </td>
                <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 10px;">
                    <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Formative Assessment Strategy:</b> Teacher observation checklist and Peer Assessment (for the mediator's effectiveness). (7 min)</p>
                    <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Assessment Task:</b> Students participate in the group planning and mediation simulation. The teacher uses a checklist to observe individual students' mediation skills, while peers use a simple rubric to evaluate the designated mediator's performance during their group's challenge.</p>
                    <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Evaluation Criteria (Teacher & Peer Checklist):</b></p>
                    <ul style="margin-bottom: 4px; padding-left: 20px;">
                        <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">Rephrases statements clearly to resolve misunderstandings (e.g., "Mindfulness means *focusing* on the present moment to *reduce stress*.").</li>
                        <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">Uses gestures or visuals effectively to guide focus (e.g., demonstrates a calming hand gesture).</li>
                        <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">Politely aids in negotiating group roles with examples (e.g., "Would you like to cover *relaxation techniques*?").</li>
                        <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">Clarifies group goals using examples (e.g., refers to Parque Natural Metropolitano).</li>
                        <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">Uses target grammar (gerunds, modals for advice, present continuous for trends) and vocabulary accurately.</li>
                        <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">Pronunciation of /uː/ and multisyllabic words is generally intelligible.</li>
                    </ul>
                    <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Student Self-Assessment / Exit Ticket:</b> (3 min)</p>
                    <ul style="margin-bottom: 4px; padding-left: 20px;">
                        <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">1. "What was one specific phrase or gesture you used today to help a classmate understand a wellness practice or project detail better?"</li>
                        <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">2. "How did you help your group ensure everyone understood their responsibilities for the 'Stress Management Video Tutorial' project?"</li>
                    </ul>
                </td>
                <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 10px;"></td>
            </tr>
            <tr style="border: 1px dashed #333;">
                <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 10px;">
                    <b style="color: #1a5276;">STAGE 6 — Reflection</b>
                </td>
                <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 10px;">
                    <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Student Self-Reflection:</b></p>
                    <ul style="margin-bottom: 4px; padding-left: 20px;">
                        <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">1. "What did I learn today about being an effective mediator in a group project, especially when discussing wellness practices like 'Forest Bathing and Other Biohacks'?"</li>
                        <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">2. "How can I apply these mediation skills to future collaborative tasks, not just in English class but in other subjects or even my daily life for *managing stress*?"</li>
                    </ul>
                    <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Teacher Reflection:</b></p>
                    <ul style="margin-bottom: 4px; padding-left: 20px;">
                        <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">Did students effectively resolve misunderstandings and negotiate roles in their groups during the project planning simulation?</li>
                        <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">Were the target grammar structures (gerunds, modals, present continuous) and vocabulary naturally integrated into their mediation and discussions?</li>
                        <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">What adjustments might be needed for the next time we engage in complex collaborative projects, particularly in reinforcing clearer communication strategies and the use of visuals/bilingual support?</li>
                        <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">How can I further encourage students to utilize their full range of linguistic and pragmatic skills when mediating information?</li>
                    </ul>
                    <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Connection to next lesson:</b> This concludes our unit on "Managing Stress in Changing Times" and the development of our "Stress Management Video Tutorial." In our next theme, we will explore [New Theme: e.g., "The Future of Work and Technology"], applying our collaborative and communication skills to new academic and vocational challenges.</p>
                </td>
                <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 10px;"></td>
            </tr>
        </tbody>
    </table>